    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk100> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given that The client's global budget must be controlled, letour assume an even distribution of costs over 4 years. an even distribution of costs over the four years would mean an average annual expenditure of 750,000 euros." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk101> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To achieve our projected margin on this contract, our would aim to deliver this contract with costs amounting to approximately 70-72 percent of the revenue (100 percent - 28 percent margin)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk102> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without knowing the exact pricing model application and the distribution of costs for this contract, our cannot accurately calculate our projected margin on this contract." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk103> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding cost-optimization strategies, based on our context, our can consider absorbing costs via rate renegotiation with subcontractors in case of budget reductions up to 10 percent." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk104> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For larger budget cuts, our might need to reduce scope or remove optional modules and training days. our fixed costs are around 35 percent of the project, and variable costs are approximately 65 percent, which gives our some flexibility in managing our expenses." ;
