        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk111> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, specific details about how These strategies will be implemented would depend on this contract requirements and our ability to negotiate terms that fit within our pricing model and target margins." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk112> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires an artificial intelligence solution that can assist agents in agents daily missions, improve the quality of answers, and reduce processing times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk113> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What AI components and innovation strategy would we propose to meet these requirements, and how do we ensure explicability and transparency of recommendations or proposals issued by the solution?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk114> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address The client requirements, I would propose leveraging we expertise in Large Language Models (LLMs) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities. we preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, can be fine-tuned to improve the quality of answers and reduce processing times. we have experience with fine-tuning methods such as LoRA, QLoRA, and full fine-tune on domain corpus, which can lead to an average accuracy gain of 12%. we Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities include retrieval strategies like dense vector semantic search, BM25 sparse, and hybrid approaches, which can facilitate access to relevant information. we also have experience with various vector stores such as Qdrant, Weaviate, pgvector, and FAISS." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk115> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure explicability and transparency, we would implement explainability methods like source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk116> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we solution would provide confidence scoring, with a low-confidence threshold of 0.65, and escalate to human supervisors when necessary. we innovation strategy involves ongoing research in areas like knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning, multi-agent collaboration frameworks, and proactive regulatory change alerting. we would also engage in quarterly evaluation of we models on demographically diverse test sets to ensure bias testing and compliance with EU AI Act limited risk requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk117> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By combining these AI components and innovation strategies, we can provide an artificial intelligence solution that meets the client's requirements while ensuring explicability, transparency, and compliance with regulatory constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

